---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RecordAnatomy from "../components/diagrams/RecordAnatomy.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sample Decision Record | BeaconGuard Assurance"
  description="Illustrative related BeaconGuard Verifiable Decision Records for request admission ALLOW and result-to-action DENY in one governed AI transaction."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h1>Sample Decision Record</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      <strong>Illustrative controlled example.</strong> Related Verifiable
      Decision Records for one governed AI transaction: request admission
      ALLOW, then result-to-action DENY. Not a real customer record and not a
      claim that every deployment will expose fields in identical presentation
      form.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Illustrative transaction outcome</h2>
    <div class="sample-record sample-record--compact">
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Request Admission</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">ALLOW</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">AI Provider Result</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Received (untrusted proposal)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Result-to-Action Authorization</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">DENY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Enterprise Effect</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Prevented</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      Provider success is not enterprise authorization. The AI-generated result
      remained an untrusted proposal. BeaconGuard denied the declared intended
      enterprise action; the enterprise application did not execute it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Record anatomy</h2>
    <p>
      Annotated field groups for related request-admission and result-to-action
      decision evidence. This is anatomy of the evidence artifacts, not a
      process diagram.
    </p>
    <RecordAnatomy />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What this sample is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Help reviewers understand what related Verifiable Decision Records
        contain across one governed transaction
      </li>
      <li>
        Show how request admission and result-to-action decisions remain
        separate immutable outcomes with shared correlation context
      </li>
      <li>
        Separate release identity, playbook identity, and decision outcomes from
        downstream business records
      </li>
      <li>Support architecture, security, risk, and audit review</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Sample A — Request Admission (illustrative)</h2>
    <div class="sample-record sample-record--compact">
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Authorization point</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Request Admission Authorization</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Decision outcome</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">ALLOW</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">release_identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">release.healthcare.ops.v12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">playbook_identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">playbook.healthcare.ops.summarize.v12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Request action</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">AI-assisted operational summary request</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Actor type</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Regulated operations user</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Correlation identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">txn.illustrative.ops-summary.001</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Outcome</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Provider invocation permitted</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Sample B — Result-to-Action (illustrative)</h2>
    <div class="sample-record sample-record--compact">
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Authorization point</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Result-to-Action Authorization</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Decision outcome</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">DENY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Reason code (illustrative)</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">APPROVAL_REQUIRED</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">release_identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">release.healthcare.ops.v12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">playbook_identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">playbook.healthcare.ops.summarize.v12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">AI-generated result status</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Received; untrusted proposal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Intended enterprise action</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Write operational summary into care workflow</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Correlation identity</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">txn.illustrative.ops-summary.001</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Decision reason</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Required precondition approval absent; enterprise effect prevented</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Review obligation</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Privacy governance notification (does not permit execution)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-record-row">
        <span class="sample-record-label">Enterprise effect</span>
        <span class="sample-record-value">Prevented</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      The illustrative reason <code>APPROVAL_REQUIRED</code> means a required
      precondition approval is absent for the declared action. It is not the
      privileged-review reason <code>REVIEW_REQUIRED</code> shown in The
      BeaconGuard Review Process demonstration. Review does not mutate this DENY
      into ALLOW.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What reviewers should notice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Related request and action decisions share correlation context and keep
        separate immutable outcomes
      </li>
      <li>
        Runtime permission results are ALLOW or DENY only; absent approval is
        DENY, not a permission-to-execute review state
      </li>
      <li>
        An AI-generated result can be received and still leave enterprise effect
        prevented
      </li>
      <li>
        release_identity and playbook_identity support reconstruction against
        the Active Verified Release
      </li>
      <li>
        A review obligation may notify governance; it does not change the DENY
        result
      </li>
      <li>
        Downstream systems remain responsible for business-state and transaction
        authority
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Next step</h2>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/reviewer-kit">Return to Reviewer Kit</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/proof-evidence">View more evidence samples</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/verification">Open Verification</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
